  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Sunday)\nIssued at 1048 AM MDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\n16z surface analysis had a low over northeastern WY with a couple\nof troughs; one south into CO and another east into eastern SD. \nSustained east/southeast flow over western SD bringing increasing \nmoisture to the area. Water vapour loop has upper ridge centered \nover NM with ridge axis into the northern Plains. Shortwave \nevident over northwest WY, ready to overtop the ridge and cross \nthe CWA during peak insolation this afternoon/evening. That will \nbe the main short term concern.\n\nThis afternoon/tonight, 1-2KJ/kg SBCAPE develops along the \naforementioned boundaries with similar amounts of DCAPE. Effective\nshear forecast to be 30-45kts as shortwave crosses. CAMs show \nconvective initiation by 20z, focused on the higher terrain \ninitially and then the surface boundaries as SBCIN erodes. \nClusters of storms will move east, potentially with congealing \ncold pools, increasing the damaging wind threat. CAMs show a \ncouple clusters of enhanced wind gusts. Thunderstorms end \novernight. Temperatures will be near guidance, but below heat \nheadline criteria.\n\nTuesday looks less active right now given shortwave ridging and \nlack of a distinct shortwave moving through the area, but would \nstill expect some convection tied to the terrain. Wednesday, \nensemble guidance shows another distinct wave moving across the \narea during peak heating resulting in an elevated risk of severe \nweather. Temperatures remain hot, but below heat headlines \ncriteria.\n\nThe rest of the forecast will be dominated by the upper ridge over \nthe central CONUS and hot weather. There will be waves kicking off a \nfew storms from time-to-time. If you believe the long term ensemble \nguidance, someone of a cooldown may develop next week, but \nconfidence low.",
